d 'PATHINTDID': module performing Path-Integrated Difference-in-Differences (PI-DiD): Identification, Estimation, and Inference
d
d  In empirical policy evaluation, interventions such as worker
d training programs, cash transfers, localized health programs, and
d digital financial services often produce dynamic, transitory
d effects where individual outcome paths temporarily diverge from
d counterfactuals before converging again due to skill depreciation
d or control-group catch-up. Standard Difference-in-Differences
d models suffer from endpoint-subtraction bias because they
d evaluate policy efficacy using static endline snapshot contrasts,
d which can erroneously indicate zero impact when trajectories
d rejoin despite substantial historical utility generated while the
d program was active. The pathintdid package overcomes this
d limitation by implementing a path-integrated framework that
d measures the total net stock of accumulated welfare generated
d over the post-treatment window by integrating the area trapped
d between realized and counterfactual outcome trajectories. This
d cumulative impact is also scaled into an annualized per-unit
d treatment flow, providing an accurate metric of policy success
d under dynamic rejoining conditions while accounting for arbitrary
d within-unit temporal correlation through cluster-robust standard
d errors. 
d
d KW: difference in differences
d KW: DiD
d KW: path integration
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260726
d
d Author: Comlan Apollinaire-Fabrice Salavi,  African School of Economics, Benin
d Support: email  fsalavi@@africanschoolofeconomics.com
d
f pathintdid.ado
f pathintdid.sthlp
f pathintdidplot.ado
f pathintdidrobust.ado
f pathintdidrobust.sthlp
f ../e/example_pathintdid.do
f ../t/trainingpanel.dta
